# demo-app

Rust core packaged as a debug Android APK (com.example.demo_app) for arm64-v8a and x86_64.

The host build and tests need no Android SDK:

```sh
bazel build //...
bazel test //...
```

The APK and its launchers are tagged manual. They need an installed Android SDK
with platform android-34, build-tools 35.0.0 and an NDK:

```sh
export ANDROID_HOME=$HOME/Android/Sdk
export ANDROID_SDK_ROOT=$ANDROID_HOME
export ANDROID_NDK_REVISION=<installed ndk version>
bazel build --config=android :demo-app_apk_file
bazel test --config=android :demo-app_check_test
bazel run --config=android :demo-app_install
bazel run --config=android :demo-app_start
bazel run --config=android :demo-app_log
```

The launchers name emulator-5554. The APK is debug-signed, so no keys are needed.
The app ID, ABIs and API level are attributes of `:demo-app_apk` in BUILD.bazel.
